      "source": [
        "# Digital Design - mod-18\n\n",
        "**Course:** digital-design\n\n",
        "Run the code cells below to practice.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "4-bit Ripple Up Counter (using T flip-flops, T=1):\n\nCLK \u2192 [T-FF0] \u2192 [T-FF1] \u2192 [T-FF2] \u2192 [T-FF3]\n       Q0 \u2197       Q1 \u2197       Q2 \u2197       Q3\n     (toggles    (toggles    (toggles    (toggles\n     on CLK)    on Q0 fall) on Q1 fall) on Q2 fall)"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "4-bit Synchronous Up Counter:\n\nCLK \u2192 [T-FF0] \u2192 [T-FF1] \u2192 [T-FF2] \u2192 [T-FF3]\n       T0=1      T1=Q0    T2=Q0Q1   T3=Q0Q1Q2\n\nRule: Bit i toggles when all lower bits are 1"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "T0 = 1           (always toggles)\nT1 = Q0          (toggles when Q0=1)\nT2 = Q0 & Q1    (toggles when Q0=Q1=1)\nT3 = Q0 & Q1 & Q2  (toggles when Q0=Q1=Q2=1)"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "T0 = 1\nT1 = Q0'\nT2 = Q0' & Q1'\nT3 = Q0' & Q1' & Q2'"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "T0 = 1\nT1 = (DIR & Q0) | (DIR' & Q0')\nT2 = (DIR & Q0 & Q1) | (DIR' & Q0' & Q1')\n\nWhen DIR=1: count up\nWhen DIR=0: count down"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "Method 1: Detect state 1010 (10) and force reset\n  - Use combinational logic to detect count = 10\n  - Asynchronously reset all flip-flops\n  - Problem: brief glitch at state 10\n\nMethod 2: Synchronous design with next-state logic\n  - Design state transitions so that state 9 transitions to state 0\n  - No glitches, preferred approach"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "States (4-bit ring counter): 1000 \u2192 0100 \u2192 0010 \u2192 0001 \u2192 1000\n- N flip-flops give N states (inefficient encoding)\n- Only one flip-flop is hot at any time (one-hot encoding)\n- No decoding logic needed to identify current state\n- Self-correcting versions detect and fix invalid states"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "python",
          "States (4-bit Johnson): 0000 \u2192 1000 \u2192 1100 \u2192 1110 \u2192 1111 \u2192 0111 \u2192 0011 \u2192 0001 \u2192 0000\n- N flip-flops give 2N states\n- Decoding requires only 2-input AND gates\n- Used for timing/sequencing generation"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "verilog",
          "// 4-bit Synchronous Up Counter with enable and reset\nmodule counter_4bit(\n    input  wire       clk,\n    input  wire       rst_n,\n    input  wire       enable,\n    output reg  [3:0] count,\n    output wire       terminal_count\n);\n    assign terminal_count = (count == 4'd15) & enable;\n    \n    always @(posedge clk or negedge rst_n) begin\n        if (!rst_n)\n            count <= 4'b0;\n        else if (enable)\n            count <= count + 4'b1;\n    end\nendmodule"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "verilog",
          "// Modulo-N Counter (parameterized)\nmodule mod_n_counter #(parameter N = 10, parameter WIDTH = 4)(\n    input  wire             clk,\n    input  wire             rst_n,\n    input  wire             enable,\n    output reg  [WIDTH-1:0] count,\n    output wire             rollover\n);\n    assign rollover = (count == N - 1) & enable;\n    \n    always @(posedge clk or negedge rst_n) begin\n        if (!rst_n)\n            count <= {WIDTH{1'b0}};\n        else if (enable) begin\n            if (count == N - 1)\n                count <= {WIDTH{1'b0}};\n            else\n                count <= count + 1'b1;\n        end\n    end\nendmodule"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "verilog",
          "// Up/Down Counter\nmodule up_down_counter #(parameter N = 8)(\n    input  wire         clk,\n    input  wire         rst_n,\n    input  wire         enable,\n    input  wire         direction,  // 1=up, 0=down\n    input  wire         load,\n    input  wire [N-1:0] data_in,\n    output reg  [N-1:0] count\n);\n    always @(posedge clk or negedge rst_n) begin\n        if (!rst_n)\n            count <= {N{1'b0}};\n        else if (load)\n            count <= data_in;\n        else if (enable) begin\n            if (direction)\n                count <= count + 1'b1;\n            else\n                count <= count - 1'b1;\n        end\n    end\nendmodule"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "verilog",
          "// Ring Counter\nmodule ring_counter #(parameter N = 8)(\n    input  wire       clk,\n    input  wire       rst_n,\n    output reg [N-1:0] ring\n);\n    always @(posedge clk or negedge rst_n) begin\n        if (!rst_n)\n            ring <= {{(N-1){1'b0}}, 1'b1};  // Initialize: 0...001\n        else\n            ring <= {ring[0], ring[N-1:1]};   // Rotate right\n    end\nendmodule"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        [
          "verilog",
          "// Cascaded counters: seconds/minutes timer\nmodule timer_60sec(\n    input  wire       clk_1hz,\n    input  wire       rst_n,\n    output wire [5:0] seconds,\n    output wire [5:0] minutes\n);\n    wire sec_rollover;\n    \n    mod_n_counter #(.N(60), .WIDTH(6)) sec_cnt(\n        .clk(clk_1hz), .rst_n(rst_n), .enable(1'b1),\n        .count(seconds), .rollover(sec_rollover)\n    );\n    \n    mod_n_counter #(.N(60), .WIDTH(6)) min_cnt(\n        .clk(clk_1hz), .rst_n(rst_n), .enable(sec_rollover),\n        .count(minutes), .rollover()\n    );\nendmodule"
        ]
      ]
    }
